    "text": ":brain: *Hermes (Planner)* \u2014 Sprint 3 plan\n\nSprint 3 goal: Add accountability depth to PulseDesk \u2014 make every ticket action traceable, time-bound, and surfaced, all within the existing org-scoped tenancy.\nIssues:\n1. Ticket activity log / audit trail \u2014 new TicketActivity model recording events (created, status_changed, assigned, replied) with actor + timestamp, org-scoped via BelongsToOrganization; GET /tickets/{ticket}/activity endpoint; Pest tenancy test. One PR.\n2. SLA policies &amp; timers \u2014 SlaPolicy table mapping priority to first-response/resolution targets; stamp due_at on ticket creation; breach flag. One PR.\n3. In-app notifications \u2014 notify assignee/requester on reply + assignment; list/unread endpoint. One PR.\nAssignment -&gt; OpenClaw: Issue 1 \u2014 Ticket activity log. Branch: feature/ticket-activity-log.\nBuild: migration + backend/app/Models/TicketActivity.php using the BelongsToOrganization trait (every query org-scoped from the session \u2014 never trust a client id). Columns: ticket_id, actor_id, event (created|status_changed|assigned|replied), meta json, timestamps. Wire events through Eloquent observers on Ticket + TicketReply so creation, status/assignee changes, and replies all log automatically.\nAdd GET /tickets/{ticket}/activity in TicketController, newest-first.\nTest (Pest): user sees own org's events; cross-org ticket's activity returns 403/empty. Run: cd backend &amp;&amp; php artisan test \u2014 must be green.\nOpen a PR to main (I merge). No secrets in the diff. Post your report to #agent-coder as: What I Did / What's Left / What Needs Your Call.",
